  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "CM01112",
    "sub_id": "63000",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "Assessment Methods\tAction\n(1)\tMidterm: 15%\n(2)\tGroup Presentation: 15%\n(3)\tParticipation & In-class group discussion: 20%\n(4)\tAttendance: 10%\nNo points will be deducted for absences in the first five classes, and from the sixth class onwards, 0.5 points will be deducted from the total score for each class until 10 points are deducted.\n(5)\tFinal Exams:10%\n(6)\tFinal Report Presentation: 30%\n(7)\tBonus: five additional points",
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>(1) Midterm: 15% (2) Group Presentation: 15% (3) Participation &amp; In-class group discussion: 20% (4) Attendance: 10% No points will be deducted for absences in the first five classes, and from the sixth class onwards, 0.5 points will be deducted from the total score for each class until 10 points are deducted. (5) Final Exams:10% (6) Final Report Presentation: 30% (7) Bonus: five additional points</div>\n",
    "course_pol": "課堂上的行為始終應要及時、要專業、要做好準備、要有禮貌。同學、教師或其他講師間，應保有彼此尊嚴和相互尊重，才能進行有效的學習。為了確保有利於學習環境，冀望每個人都能做到以下幾點，彼此遵守課堂行為規則，習慣禮貌的文化。",
    "course_pol_en": "All course activities will be carried out in an atmosphere of friendly participation and interaction among students, respecting and appreciating each student's personal experience, background and perspectives, such as various school systems at home and abroad, diverse enrollment and learning cultures, gender, etc. You are expected to apply the highest academic standards throughout this course and to treat fellow students with dignity and respect.",
    "course_rem": "多樣化、公平和包容性聲明 我的教學設計，要讓來自不同背景和觀點的學生都能從這門課程中獲得很好的學習，學生的學習需求能得到解決，學生帶給這門課的多樣性可以經舉手、邀請您合適地表達出來，並被視為一種資源、力量並惠及所有學生。如有任何疑慮，請利用請益時間來找我。",
    "course_rem_en": "Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Statement I design my instruction so that students from different backgrounds and perspectives can learn well from the course, that the learning needs of the students are addressed, and that the diversity that students bring to the course can be met with a raise of hand, invitation You are appropriately expressed and seen as a resource, strength and benefit to all students. If you have any concerns, please take advantage of the time to come to me.",
    "ais_meno": "<div>學習必須以誠信為基礎，任何學生企圖將自己未製作的作品，作為自己的作品，此行為是為不誠實行為。在作業、測驗或考試中作弊或抄襲的學生或協助他人的行為，該次成績以零分計，若是累犯，將依逢甲大學學生獎懲辦法提送。</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>In the special report, observe and review the learning tasks of the students, and encourage cooperation with the students to complete the written report or the project practice. Forming study or reading groups can be an effective way to learn. However, when you write an article or thesis, the words must be your own.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": null
  },
